operations.description:
Delete an icon
Delete an existing icon by its unique id.
DELETE /icon/api/icons/{id}

Download an icon
Download an existing icon by its unique id.
GET /icon/api/icons/{id}

Find a catalog item with specified ID.
Returns the catalog item with the specified ID.
GET /catalog/api/items/{id}

Get a response with upfront prices for a given catalog item.
Returns upfront prices of a given catalog item.
GET /catalog/api/items/{id}/upfront-prices/{upfrontPriceId}

Fetch detailed catalog item version.
Returns a detailed catalog item version.
GET /catalog/api/items/{id}/versions/{versionId}

Submit action on requests. Allowable values: cancel, dismiss.
Cancel can be submitted on In-progress requests and Dismiss can be submitted on Failed requests.
POST /deployment/api/requests/{requestId}

Delete a deployment. Effectively triggers a Delete Day2 operation
Deletes the deployment with the supplied ID, cleans up the associated resources from the Cloud Provider.
DELETE /deployment/api/deployments/{deploymentId}

Delete resource associated with a deployment. Effectively triggers a Delete Day2 operation.
Deletes the resource with the specified ID and attempts to delete resource from the Cloud Provider.
DELETE /deployment/api/deployments/{deploymentId}/resources/{resourceId}

Fetch deployment action.
Returns an action for the deployment specified by its Deployment ID and Action ID.
GET /deployment/api/deployments/{deploymentId}/actions/{actionId}

Fetch a specific deployment.
Returns the deployment with the supplied ID.
GET /deployment/api/deployments/{deploymentId}

Get the Request.
Returns the request with the given ID.
GET /deployment/api/requests/{requestId}

Fetch resource action.
Returns an action for the resource specified by its Resource ID and Action ID.
GET /deployment/api/deployments/{deploymentId}/resources/{resourceId}/actions/{actionId}

Fetch resource associated with a deployment.
Returns the resource with the specified ID that is correlated with the supplied deployment.
GET /deployment/api/deployments/{deploymentId}/resources/{resourceId}

Fetch a specific Resource type.
Returns the Resource type with the supplied ID.
GET /deployment/api/resource-types/{resourceTypeId}

Fetch a specific resource.
Returns the resource with the supplied ID.
GET /deployment/api/resources/{resourceId}

Fetch resource action.
Returns an action for the resource specified by its Resource ID and Action ID.
GET /deployment/api/resources/{resourceId}/actions/{actionId}

Get supervisor resource by ID
Returns a supervisor resource with the specified ID.
GET /deployment/api/supervisor-resources/{id}

Delete Subscription
Delete Subscription. Only Solution users and system admin (e.g. for vRO) can manage subscriptions.
DELETE /event-broker/api/subscriptions/{id}

Get Event by id
Retrieve the details of a specified Event.
GET /event-broker/api/events/{id}

Retrieves Event Topic
Retrieves Event Topic by id.
GET /event-broker/api/topics/{id}

Retrieves Subscription
Retrieves Subscription by id.
GET /event-broker/api/subscriptions/{id}

Delete form by ID
Delete the form with the specified ID.
DELETE /form-service/api/forms/{id}

Get form by ID
Retrieve the Form definition of a form with the specified ID.
GET /form-service/api/forms/{id}

[DEPRECATED] Gets resource type by id (DEPRECATED).
This endpoint is deprecated. Use `/deployment/api/resource-types/{id}` directly from the Catalog Service instead. Get the resource type for the provided ID in the currently authorized organization
GET /form-service/api/deployment/resource-types/{id}

Delete an integration
Delete an integration with a given id asynchronously
DELETE /iaas/api/integrations/{id}

Delete Request
Delete a single Request
DELETE /iaas/api/request-tracker/{id}

Get an integration
Get an integration with a given id
GET /iaas/api/integrations/{id}

Get request tracker
Get request tracker with a given id
GET /iaas/api/request-tracker/{id}

Update an integration
Update a single integration asynchronously
PATCH /iaas/api/integrations/{id}

Delete a policy
Delete a specified policy corresponding to its unique id.
DELETE /policy/api/policies/{id}

Returns a policy decision by id.
Find a specific policy decision based on the input policy decision id.
GET /policy/api/policyDecisions/{id}

Returns a specified policy.
Find a specific policy based on the input policy id.
GET /policy/api/policies/{id}

Returns the policy type with the specified ID.
Find a specific policy type based on the input policy type id.
GET /policy/api/policyTypes/{id}

Deletes a project
Deletes a project by id.
DELETE /project-service/api/projects/{id}

Retrieves a project
Retrieves a project by id.
GET /project-service/api/projects/{id}

Get secrets accessible to the current user for a project
Returns secrets (both project-scoped and org-scoped) for the specified project if the user has PROJECT_ADMIN role. Returns only name and description of secrets.
GET /platform/api/secrets/project-secrets/{projectId}

Modifies a project
Modifies a project by id. Fields that can be modified: name, description, constraints, properties, cost, operation timeout, shared resources.
PATCH /project-service/api/projects/{id}

Remove certificate library item.
Delete the specified certificate library item. Only items that are not in use can be deleted. Note: This API also supports a former (erroneously spelt) alternate path /cetificateLibrary/{id} as a Deprecated API (deprecated-in and removed after API version 36.0)
DELETE /cloudapi/1.0.0/ssl/certificateLibrary/{id}

Delete an individual custom rights category.
Deletes the requested Custom Rights Category by id.
DELETE /cloudapi/1.0.0/rightsCategories/{id}

Deletes the defined entity with the unique identifier (URN)
Deletes the defined entity with the unique identifier (URN). A multi-stage entity deletion process can achieved using the PreDelete and PostDelete RDE lifecycle hooks. When deleting a defined entity the PreDelete hook is executed first and if invocation fails, deletion is aborted and entity remains unchanged. If PreDelete hook execution succeeds, the entity is moved into IN_DELETION state and PostDelete hook execution is started. If the PostDelete hook succeeds, the entity is deleted. Otherwise, it remains in IN_DELETION state. An entity can always be deleted by setting the invokeHooks parame…
DELETE /cloudapi/1.0.0/entities/{id}

Delete an infra policy.
Deletes an infra policy. The deletion is performed asynchronously and returns a task.
DELETE /cloudapi/v1/infraPolicies/{urn}

Deletes a specific OIDC relying party.
Delete a specific OIDC relying party.
DELETE /cloudapi/1.0.0/openIdProvider/relyingParties/{id}

Delete an individual custom right.
Deletes the requested Custom Right by id.
DELETE /cloudapi/1.0.0/rights/{id}

Get a description of a theme to be applied. The response contains relative URLs to each file comprising the theme in the requested flavor. All mandatory resources are included, even if the theme does…
Get a description of a theme to be applied. The response contains relative URLs to each file comprising the theme in the requested flavor. All mandatory resources are included, even if the theme does not explicitly define such flavor(in which case the main flavor is used). To fetch each file, build a URL from `filesRoot` + `files[i]` and GET it. This resource is accessible without authentication.
GET /cloudapi/v1/themes/active/{orgName}/{flavor}

Get a description of a theme to be applied. The response contains relative URLs to each file comprising the theme in its main flavor. To fetch each file, build a URL from `filesRoot` + `files[i]` and…
Get a description of a theme to be applied. The response contains relative URLs to each file comprising the theme in its main flavor. To fetch each file, build a URL from `filesRoot` + `files[i]` and GET it. This resource is accessible without authentication.
GET /cloudapi/v1/themes/active/{orgName}

Get specified certificate
Get the PEM-encoded certificate with the requested URN
GET /cloudapi/1.0.0/ssl/trustedCertificates/{trustedCertificate}

Get the specified certificate library item
Retrieves the specified certificate library item. Note: This API also supports a former (erroneously spelt) alternate path /cetificateLibrary/{id} as a Deprecated API (deprecated-in and removed after API version 36.0)
GET /cloudapi/1.0.0/ssl/certificateLibrary/{id}

Gets the collection of defined entities for the provider management-defined type with the specified vendor, nss and version.
Gets the collection of defined entities for the provider management-defined type with the specified vendor, nss and version. The version can act as a wildcard. If only '1' is specified as the version, all entity types with a major version of '1' will be matched (e.g. 1.0.0, 1.1.2). If '1.0' is specified, all entity types with a major version of '1' and a minor version of '0' will be included (e.g. 1.0.0, 1.0.1). If the full semver is specified, then no search will be performed. Depending on the requested items per page, and the number of returned entities, one or more metadata summary cursor …
GET /cloudapi/1.0.0/entities/types/{vendor}/{nss}/{version}

Gets the collection of defined entities for the provider management-defined type with the specified id.
Gets the collection of defined entities for the provider management-defined type with the specified id. Depending on the requested items per page, and the number of returned entities, one or more metadata summary cursor links will be returned in the headers. In order to retrieve the summaries of all the entities, clients need to fetch each separate cursor and merge the results.
GET /cloudapi/1.0.0/entities/types/{typeId}

Gets the collection of defined entities for the provider management-defined type with the specified vendor and nss.
Gets the collection of defined entities for the provider management-defined type with the specified vendor and nss without restrictions on the version.
GET /cloudapi/1.0.0/entities/types/{vendor}/{nss}

Gets the collection of defined entities for the provider management-defined interface with the specified vendor, nss and version
Gets the collection of defined entities for the provider management-defined interface with the specified vendor, nss and version. The version can act as a wildcard. If only '1' is specified as the version, all entity types with a major version of '1' will be matched (e.g. 1.0.0, 1.1.2). If '1.0' is specified, all entity types with a major version of '1' and a minor version of '0' will be included (e.g. 1.0.0, 1.0.1). If the full semver is specified, then no search will be performed. Depending on the requested items per page, and the number of returned entities, one or more metadata summary cu…
GET /cloudapi/1.0.0/entities/interfaces/{vendor}/{nss}/{version}

Gets the collection of defined entities for the provider management-defined interface with the specified id
Gets the collection of defined entities for the provider management-defined interface with the specified id. Depending on the requested items per page, and the number of returned entities, one or more metadata summary cursor links will be returned in the headers. In order to retrieve the summaries of all the entities, clients need to fetch each separate cursor and merge the results.
GET /cloudapi/1.0.0/entities/interfaces/{interfaceId}

Get an infra policy.
Retrieves a specific infra policy by its URN.
GET /cloudapi/v1/infraPolicies/{urn}

Get a Behavior in the Defined Interface.
Retrieve a specific Behavior in the specified Defined Interface.
GET /cloudapi/1.0.0/interfaces/{id}/behaviors/{behaviorId}

Get a Namespace
Retrieves the specified namespace
GET /cloudapi/v1/namespaces/{namespaceUrn}

Retrieves a specific OIDC relying party.
Get a specific OIDC relying party.
GET /cloudapi/1.0.0/openIdProvider/relyingParties/{id}

Retrieves a Region.
Retrieves a region with the given ID.
GET /cloudapi/v1/regions/{regionUrn}

Retrieve an individual right.
Retrieves the requested Right by id.
GET /cloudapi/1.0.0/rights/{id}

Retrieve an individual Right category.
Retrieves the requested Rights Category by id.
GET /cloudapi/1.0.0/rightsCategories/{id}

Get a Behavior in the Defined Type
Retrieve a specific Behavior in the Defined Type. The Behavior must be specified by ID.
GET /cloudapi/1.0.0/entityTypes/{id}/behaviors/{behaviorId}

Get a specified user by id. If the id of a service account is specified instead, a simplified view of the service account is returned instead.
Get a specified user by id.
GET /cloudapi/1.0.0/users/{userUrn}

Get a vCenter compute policy.
Retrieves a specific vCenter compute policy by its URN.
GET /cloudapi/v1/vCenterComputePolicies/{urn}

Get a VirtualMachineClass
Retrieves the specified virtualMachineClass
GET /cloudapi/v1/virtualMachineClasses/{virtualMachineClassUrn}

Retrieve a specific Zone.
Retrieves a Zone.
GET /cloudapi/v1/zones/{zoneUrn}

Update the specified certificate library item.
Updates the specified certificate library item. Only the alias and description fields may be edited Note: This API also supports a former (erroneously spelt) alternate path /cetificateLibrary/{id} as a Deprecated API (deprecated-in and removed after API version 36.0)
PUT /cloudapi/1.0.0/ssl/certificateLibrary/{id}

Update specified content library
Update content library.
PUT /cloudapi/v1/contentLibraries/{libraryUrn}

Updates the defined entity with the unique identifier (URN)
Update the defined entity with the unique identifier (URN). This operation can also be used to upgrade/downgrade the entity to a different version of the defined entity type it is an instance of by setting the "entityType" property. The update operation may change the entityState of the Defined Entity. If the entity's entityState is: - PRE_CREATED before the update - the entity will remain in PRE_CREATED entityState after the update - RESOLUTION_ERROR before the update - the entity will move to PRE_CREATED entityState after the update - IN_DELETION before the update - the entity will remain i…
PUT /cloudapi/1.0.0/entities/{id}

Modify the details of the specified group.
Modify details of the specified group.
PUT /cloudapi/1.0.0/groups/{groupUrn}

Update an infra policy.
Updates an existing infra policy.
PUT /cloudapi/v1/infraPolicies/{urn}

Updates a specific OIDC relying party.
Updates an OIDC relying party.
PUT /cloudapi/1.0.0/openIdProvider/relyingParties/{id}

Updates an organization.
Updates an organization. If the managedBy field is being updated, the operation is asynchronous and a task is returned in the location header. Otherwise, the operation is synchronous.
PUT /cloudapi/1.0.0/orgs/{orgUrn}

Update a specific token
Update a token
PUT /cloudapi/1.0.0/tokens/{id}

Modify the details of a user. A non-administrator user may only modify their own password. An administrator can edit any user.
Modify basic details of the specified user.
PUT /cloudapi/1.0.0/users/{userUrn}

Get aggregated information for a workflow
Get a workflow with a specific ID
GET /vro/aggregated-workflows/{id}

Find Workflow Run by run ID
Retrieves the Workflow Run for the specific run ID
GET /vro/runs/{runId}
